    <item>
      <title>HENRY DAVID THOREAU</title>
      <link>https://www.kpbs.org/news/2026/03/05/henry-david-thoreau</link>
      <description>Premieres Monday, March 30, 2026 from 9 - 11 p.m. on KPBS TV + Tuesday, March 31 at 9 p.m. / Stream with KPBS+. Henry David Thoreau helped define modern environmentalism and nonviolent resistance, yet his life has been obscured by myth. The author of Walden and Civil Disobedience, he was brilliant but flawed, idealistic but opinionated. A writer, scientist and activist, his words resonate urgently with today’s challenges as humanity looks for ways to live in harmony with nature—and each other.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.kpbs.org/news/2026/03/05/henry-david-thoreau</guid>
      <enclosure url="https://cdn.kpbs.org/dims4/default/33e4403/2147483647/strip/false/crop/1802x1802+68+0/resize/600x600!/quality/90/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fkpbs-brightspot.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com%2F62%2Fa7%2F326b6b4644c2acfff88087e06cea%2Fhenry-david-thoreau-henry-david-thoreau.jpg" length="0" type="image/jpeg"/>
